{"h": {"measure": "R", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 104, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing a 3x3 conv on the edge into the output deletes the main learnable feature path, so it hurts far more than removing a parameter-free edge (exp 1, 18 vs 49)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing an avg-pool on the direct input-to-output edge with a conv removes a harmful smoothing shortcut and adds capacity, giving large gains (exp 8, 22)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a 3x3 conv for pooling on the direct input-output edge loses a key conv path and degrades accuracy much more than swapping a skip (exp 32, 86 vs 11, 95)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 2->3 is absent, edge 1->3 is one of few routes to the output, so putting a conv there matters much more (exp 42, 67)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "If the path into node 1 already has a 3x3 conv, the cell already has learnable capacity, so adding another conv on edge 5 yields smaller gains (exp 24 vs 13, 30, 39)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 0 hurts more when it carries a conv than when it is a skip, which is nearly redundant with edge 3 (exp 5 vs 25, 55, 88)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "With no direct input-output edge, information must flow through node 2, so a conv on edge 1 contributes more (exp 23, 53 vs 59, 69, 93)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a conv on edge 1->3 with parameter-free pooling removes capacity, whereas replacing a skip or none changes little."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 5 is cut, the direct edge 0->3 carries more of the output signal, so making it a conv gives a bigger boost (exp 17)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Turning a 3x3 conv into an identity on the final edge sacrifices learnable capacity, while replacing pooling or none with skip is neutral or positive (exp 6, 56)."}], "tok": 17453, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "none"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [0, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [4, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1"], [2, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [0, "none"]], [["none", "none", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [5, "skip_connect"]], [["skip_connect", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [1, "skip_connect"]], [["avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_1x1"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3"], [0, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [4, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "none", "skip_connect"], [3, "avg_pool_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "avg_pool_3x3